hological assessment of the response of locally advanced breast cancer to neoadjuvant chemotherapy and its implications for surgical management</article-title><source>Surg Today</source><year>2000</year><volume>30</volume><fpage>249</fpage><lpage>254</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Surg Today||30|249||bib11|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10752778</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Elston</surname><given-names>CW</given-names></name><name><surname>Ellis</surname><given-names>IO</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Pathological prognostic factors in breast cancer. I. The value of histological grade in breast cancer: experience from a large study with long-term follow-up</article-title><source>Histopathology</source><year>1991</year><volume>19</volume><fpage>403</fpage><lpage>410</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Histopathology||19|403||bib12|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1757079</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Esserman</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Hylton</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Yassa</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Barclay</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Frankel</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Sickles</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Utility of magnetic resonance imaging in the management of breast cancer: evidence for improved preoperative staging &#x0005b;In Process Citation&#x0005d;</article-title><source>J Clin Oncol</source><year>1999</year><volume>17</volume><fpage>110</fpage><lpage>119</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'J Clin Oncol||17|110||bib13|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10458224</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-